 "method": "Guided review on 2026-11-22 from a read-only Spec Kit analyze/converge/checklist pass over the frozen candidate: Outcome table against gate1-a0 and gate1-v3-a0prime evidence, Wilson intervals recomputed (95/100 [0.888, 0.978]; 91/100 [0.838, 0.952]), 0/3 prompt reviews, T007/T008/T009 cancellation hashes against github-tracking.json, a credential and content scan of evidence and reviews, and the T016 errata (A0' skill hash 8fb7c5cd, the two protocol deviations) applied before the re-freeze.",
 "humanReview": {
  "decision": "approved",
  "date": "2026-11-22",
  "rationale": "Approve SPEC-078 as a completed research protocol with a negative result: A0 (95/100 on v2-test) and A0' (91/100 on v3-test) both miss OD-1 only through the no-0/3-prompt clause; H-A0 and H-A0' are not supported and H-G2 was not tested. Accepted limits as documented: v3 independence rests on the mechanical checks because three v2-test prompts were read before v3 was built; the five 0/3 prompts are accepted as model failures; results cover one host, one model and synthetic held-out prompts only. This approval does not certify real-world reliability of analyze-work: the tool-level kind fix, a fresh held-out split and a real-session shadow check with a preregistered threshold belong to the follow-up spec, and analyze-work stays advisory until then."
 },
